new 14 and 16 inch MacBook Pros with the  new M2 Pro and M2 Max chips have finally  been revealed through a press release  and not only that but the Mac Mini has  also just been updated with M2 and M2  Pro chip options finally replacing the  old Intel model so in this video I'm  gonna go through all of the new details  and give you guys my own recommendations  on whether it's worth actually upgrading  to any of them right now or waiting for  the M3 chip family models so let's get  right into it now of course with the new  Macbook Pros we have the same 14 and 16  inch models with the M2 Pro and M2 Max  upgraded chips those are five nanometer  chips from tsmc unfortunately we did not  get an upgrade to the four nanometer  which definitely sucks it finally got  upgraded to up to 96 gigs of RAM which  is absolutely insane I do not recommend  that the common person goes that high it  is over kill but a nice upgrade is that  we finally have Wi-Fi 6E that is nice  and Bluetooth 5.3 to match up to the  newer iPhones and airpods pro 2. as far  as the HDMI port we finally have HDMI  2.1 which is what we needed from the  very beginning thankfully with the  efficiency updates we did get an  improvement for the battery life we have  18 hours on the 14 inch and 22 hours on  the 16 inch which is one extra hour each  for video playback which honestly isn't  that much if it was on three nanometer  it would have been a lot better but it  looks like we have to wait for the three  nanometer M3 Pro and M3 Max chips in  about a year and a half and as far as  the storage we have the same eight  terabyte storage limit just like we had  before but in terms of everything else  like the design it's basically identical  it looks the same the same shape same  every everything same displays no  difference there it's basically the same  with the ports everything else it's a  little bit disappointing but thankfully  the price is the same two thousand  dollars for the 14 inch and 2500 for the  16 inch so it's nice that it's at least  the same price and you get those  upgraded specs and chips and now let's  move on to the Mac Mini which hasn't  been updated in Forever literally the M1  Mac Mini in November of 2020 was the  last Mac Mini update and people have  been waiting so long for the M2 version  but now it gets even better because you  can either get the M2 Chip or the M2 Pro  which is a lot of performance packed  into the Mac Mini but other than that  not much has changed we have the same  design the same exact chassis basically  the same ports with two Thunderbolt  ports for the M2 Chip it model and four  of them on the M2 pro model and that is  replacing the Intel model finally I  don't even know why Apple was selling it  probably because they needed to have a  four port model for those who wanted it  now as far as the M2 Chip base model Mac  Mini you have between 8 to 24 gigs of  RAM between 256 and 2 terabytes of  storage but the craziest thing is the  pricing the new M2 Mac Mini is only  599 a hundred dollars cheaper than the  M1 model and you can get it as low as  4.99 with the educational discount that  is absolutely insane they're gonna kill  the low end PC market now the real  Banger is the M2 Pro Mac Mini and that  one gets a lot more performance finally  in a Mac Mini and of course the cooling  should be just fine because I don't know  if you know this or not but the M1 model  it barely used half of the internal  space of the Mac Mini so it's going to  be just fine with the M2 Pro chip now  this one can go up to eight terabytes of  storage which is a ton in that little  Mac Mini machine you now have four  Thunderbolt ports and basically it has  the same specs and features as the M2  Pro MacBook Pro and all those options  are basically the same and as far as the  pricing we have  1299 which is an absolutely killer deal  for getting an M2 Pro chip because the  only other way you're getting that is if  you're paying the two thousand dollar  price tag for the 14 inch model so for  only thirteen hundred dollars that is a  ton of performance so overall the  updates that we got today are pretty  basic which is why it's a press release  with basically nothing changing in terms  of the designs or the display features  on the MacBook Pros and even the ports  are basically unchanged just getting  small up updates but in terms of if you  should upgrade or not here is my honest  opinion I actually own a 16 inch M1 Max  MacBook Pro right now at home and I'm  definitely not going to upgrade because  the main thing that matters to me is the  design the display the feature set all  of that and obviously it hasn't really  changed at all and in terms of the  performance mine already handles  everything that I can throw at it photo  editing video editing everything else  it's just fine so I don't really see a  point in upgrading just for the faster  chips and since the battery life has  barely improved even that aspect of it  isn't really a big deal so in my opinion  nobody that owns an M1 Pro or Max  MacBook Pro should be upgrading now the  biggest issue in terms of upgrading to  these machines is that the new M2 Pro  and M2 Max are still on second gen 5  nanometer and the previous versions the  14 inch with the M1 Max overheated and  thermal throttled so much so that the  high-end 14 inch was slower than the  lower end 16 inch in some tasks that was  embarrassing and now it's gonna be even  worse with the new M2 Max 14 inch so  keep that in mind and wait until we do  our testing now if you skipped out on  all of the Apple silicon MacBooks then  that definitely changes things and if  you're ready to purchase now then  definitely do it as these are upgraded  with modern specs however if you can  wait another year and a half and be just  fine with your current MacBook or even  if you wait until the end of the year  for the regular M3 MacBook Air then I  would honestly wait because the M3  family of chips will be a lot better in  terms of efficiency and performance  thanks to three nanometer chips from  tsmc now as far as the Mac Mini that new  M2 pro model is an absolutely killer  deal in terms of performance and value  and it could even be worth upgrading  from the M1 Mac Mini if you have that  right now and definitely from any intel  model this thing is honestly the best  bang for the buck map you can get with  high performance and I would even  recommend this over the Max studio for a  lot of people out there because of the  crazy good price so there you guys have  it hopefully you enjoyed this video and  let me know down in the comments what  you think about today's announcements  from Apple and if you want to get a  better deal on the M1 Pro 14 inch right  now instead of waiting you can use the  YouTube tagging feature to check it out  and click that Circle above to subscribe  for more videos like this one especially  when we start benchmarking these new  Macs thanks for watching and we'll see  you in the next video  foreign
 

